# Optional scancode -> Linux keycode mappings, applied at boot by
# pivista-input.service. Most USB/Bluetooth remotes already emit standard
# KEY_LEFT/RIGHT/UP/DOWN/ENTER/BACK/HOMEPAGE codes and need no entries here.
#
# Find a scancode with:  sudo evtest /dev/input/eventN
# Find keycode numbers in: /usr/include/linux/input-event-codes.h
#
# Example (Amazon Fire TV remote volume rocker on some IR receivers):
# 0x1c0 172   # KEY_HOMEPAGE
